{"name":"Boiling Magma","hex":"#ff3300","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"boiling","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["present participle and gerund of boil"]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The process of changing the state of a substance from liquid to gas by heating it to its boiling point.","The cooking (of food) or cleaning (of an object) by immersing it in liquid (usually water) that is boiling."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/boiling"},{"term":"magma","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A mixture of molten silicate rock, crystals, and gas within the earth, which may be erupted as lava or cool in place to form igneous intrusions.","A basic algebraic structure consisting of a set equipped with a single binary operation."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/magma"}],"entries":[{"title":"Boiling","blocks":[{"text":"Boiling or ebullition is the rapid phase transition from liquid to gas or vapour; the reverse of boiling is condensation. Boiling occurs when a liquid is heated to its boiling point, so that the vapour pressure of the liquid is equal to the pressure exerted on the liquid by the surrounding atmosphere. Boiling and evaporation are the two main forms of liquid vapourization."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Boilingkettle.jpg/330px-Boilingkettle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boiling","wikidata":"Q41716"},{"title":"Magma","blocks":[{"text":"Magma is the molten or semi-molten natural material from which all igneous rocks are formed. Magma is found beneath the surface of the Earth, and evidence of magmatism has also been discovered on other terrestrial planets and some natural satellites. Besides molten rock, magma may also contain suspended crystals and gas bubbles."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/db/Earth_Internal_Structure.svg/330px-Earth_Internal_Structure.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Magma","wikidata":"Q42278"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/Flickr_-_cyclonebill_-_Pasta_%281%29.jpg/500px-Flickr_-_cyclonebill_-_Pasta_%281%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/Flickr_-_cyclonebill_-_Pasta_%281%29.jpg/1280px-Flickr_-_cyclonebill_-_Pasta_%281%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/Flickr_-_cyclonebill_-_Pasta_%281%29.jpg/500px-Flickr_-_cyclonebill_-_Pasta_%281%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Boiling pasta","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFlickr_-_cyclonebill_-_Pasta_(1).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/Single_tet.png/120px-Single_tet.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/Single_tet.png/250px-Single_tet.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/Single_tet.png/120px-Single_tet.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASingle_tet.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/Double_tet.png/120px-Double_tet.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/Double_tet.png/250px-Double_tet.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/Double_tet.png/120px-Double_tet.png?utm_source=e